.TH KIRIGLYPH 1 "" "Kiriglyph" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kiriglyph \- select and copy text from anything on screen, or cut out objects
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kiriglyph
[\fB\-\-background\fR | \fB\-\-select\fR | \fB\-\-quit\fR]
.br
.B kiriglyph \-\-setup
.br
.B kiriglyph \-\-version
.br
.B kiriglyph \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
Kiriglyph freezes the screen on a keyboard shortcut. Drag over text to copy
it, or click an object to cut it out as a transparent PNG. Text recognition
and object segmentation run on this computer.
.PP
Kiriglyph runs as one resident instance. Starting it again hands the request
to the running instance. It needs GNOME on Wayland and the GNOME Screenshot
portal.
.SH OPTIONS
With no option, Kiriglyph opens its window.
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start the resident instance hidden. The package starts it this way at login.
.TP
.B \-\-select
Open the selection overlay. This is the command the keyboard shortcut runs.
.TP
.B \-\-quit
Ask the running instance to quit.
.TP
.B \-\-setup
Print the first-run steps and offer to create the GNOME custom shortcut.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the Kiriglyph version.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a short usage summary.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kiriglyph/settings.json
Settings: the save folder and first-run state.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/dev.kiriglyph.Kiriglyph.desktop
Written when launch at login is switched off or on again.
.SH PRIVACY
Kiriglyph makes no network requests of its own. Working copies of the frozen
screen live in a private runtime folder and are removed when the overlay
closes. Images are saved only to the folder you choose, when you save.
.SH BUGS
Report problems at https://github.com/ne0-d/kiriglyph/issues
